    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e385ded2_daae6fd0",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3275,
      "author": {
        "id": 1237921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-17T09:24:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need this to meet carrier requirement. \n\nIn the CL you have shared, there is possibility to use apn other than user added apn in additional APN connection mode. It\u0027s a spec violation. If device fails to connect data using user added apn, device will try to connect using other apns in DB because SET_ID is not set for user added apn.",
      "parentUuid": "a4ed3941_dde002db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3275,
        "startChar": 63,
        "endLine": 3275,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "7ef4cfe0dd38274f916e6af7fa6c1475a8b34b9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b4668eb_b491c469",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3275,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-18T06:42:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on your response to the question below, we can just remove preferredApnSetId \u003d\u003d Telephony.Carriers.NO_APN_SET_ID check from buildWaitingApns. That should have the same effect. Let me know if you disagree.",
      "parentUuid": "e385ded2_daae6fd0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3275,
        "startChar": 63,
        "endLine": 3275,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "7ef4cfe0dd38274f916e6af7fa6c1475a8b34b9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c7bed9a_aa9550a4",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3275,
      "author": {
        "id": 1237921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-21T02:26:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That will not have the same effect. By removing preferredApnSetId \u003d\u003d Telephony.Carriers.NO_APN_SET_ID check from buildWaitingApns, we can exclude preset apns in additional apn connection mode. But there is still possibility that device turns off the additional APN connection mode automatically even if this connection fails to access network. For example, user may add two apns(APN1 as preferred apn and another is APN2) and their setid will be both NO_APN_SET_ID. In this case, both apns are added apnList in #buildWaitingApns. If the connection for APN1 fails to access network, the device will use APN2. We think it is a spec violation.",
      "parentUuid": "5b4668eb_b491c469",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3275,
        "startChar": 63,
        "endLine": 3275,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "7ef4cfe0dd38274f916e6af7fa6c1475a8b34b9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "544651f6_4d3fdab7",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3275,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-24T07:49:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you sure that will be spec violation? In the example you have given both are added by user so it should be ok to use the other one if the primary one does not work. They are both the same APN_SET_ID.\n\nMoreover, in the code that you have added, it is still possible that more APNs are returned as there can be multiple APNs with same value for Telephony.Carriers.APN (potentially even with different APN_SET_ID and different other parameters). That seems like a worse spec violation to me. To avoid this you can add an additional requirement in the selection string that Telephony.Carriers.APN_SET_ID \u003d Telephony.Carriers.NO_APN_SET_ID, or even better directly add a selection criteria for the row # in the database. But I would prefer to go with the former solution that I have suggested (modifying the condition in buildWaitingApns).",
      "parentUuid": "7c7bed9a_aa9550a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3275,
        "startChar": 63,
        "endLine": 3275,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "7ef4cfe0dd38274f916e6af7fa6c1475a8b34b9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
